# PART 1 — UNDERSTAND THE ICY ECOSYSTEM

Before writing code, understand these existing services and their responsibilities.

### 1. ICY Account

ICY Account is already built, including its backend.

It is the central identity and account service of the ICY ecosystem.

It manages the actual user identity and the account information associated with each user.

It is responsible for authenticating users and establishing their identity.

### 2. ICY Cloud

ICY Cloud is already built.

It provides cloud storage and other supported cloud functionality.

Do not rebuild it or create another cloud-storage service.

The ICY App Launcher Backend may later connect to its authorized interfaces when launcher functionality requires them.

### 3. ICY App Launcher

The ICY App Launcher already has an existing frontend and application interface.

It is an application launcher, not a full operating system.

It will organize, display, manage, and launch supported ICY applications and compatible third-party applications.

Its individual ICY applications will be added progressively.

### 4. New ICY App Launcher Backend

This is the component you must build now.

It will serve as the communication and application-management backend between ICY Account, the ICY App Launcher frontend, and the future application integrations.

It must have its own organized backend architecture, secure authentication verification, database integration, API routes, application registry, user-specific data management, and error-handling system.

