# PART 5 — USER PROFILE AND ACCOUNT LINKING

Create a launcher-side user identity record linked to ICY Account.

The record should use the permanent ICY Account identity identifier.

A suitable logical structure includes:

- Internal launcher record ID.
- External ICY Account subject ID.
- Display name.
- Username.
- Permitted profile image reference.
- Account-linking status.
- First successful launcher access.
- Last successful launcher access.
- Profile synchronization timestamp.
- Launcher preference reference.

Use only the fields supported by actual ICY Account responses.

The launcher must recognize returning users without making them create another account.

### Returning user process

When the same user accesses ICY App Launcher again:

- Verify the current Account session.
- Identify the account using its stable subject ID.
- Retrieve updated permitted profile information when needed.
- Load the existing launcher user record.
- Restore the user's saved launcher preferences.
- Retrieve the appropriate application catalog.
- Display the correct user's launcher environment.

If a session expires, request proper reauthentication through ICY Account.

Do not silently create a new user record whenever someone returns.

